{"kind":"assert","text":"R3b's independent read-only design review adds qualifications to the pending byte-bound question. No source edit or executable check ran.\n\nThe 50,347-byte observationBytes allowance is enforced later by serves(), not before one() inserts a shape-valid answer into reusable. Shape-valid oversized lists and strings can therefore reach the cache. one() also accepts repeated valid retained-value copies without an aggregate count bound. The proposed byte limit must measure the actual subject-name key, observation, read/last metadata and every stored value copy; the nominal maximum is not a hard pre-cache ceiling. If an oversized replacement is excluded from reuse, remove any older same-name cache entry too, so a later input cannot fall back to that older answer. Existing-name replacements should keep their FIFO position.\n\nCustody: hand() currently merges reusable lazily without pinning borrowed entries into mine. Eviction alone could remove an answer already visible to an in-flight input. I propose an input-local snapshot of Seen references when further() starts, preserving those payloads even if the global FIFO drops them. Keep the existing explicit reread when the judge asks again after a freshness/head failure; the one-answer rule prevents incidental changes by other inputs, rather than preventing that deliberate refresh. Shared Seen.last continues to track sealed use. Input-local retention is separate from the reusable-map payload bound.\n\nThe fold rejects heads below retained history, not every newer unretained cached answer. The production membershipIn/observedAt path reads the same Native object's current append-only history after eviction; monotonicity here relies on that trusted source. An arbitrary scripted port has no such promise. I propose to state this source-trust boundary explicitly, rather than add another unbounded high-water map.\n\nThe single requested signed-Native witness can seed @una, send65 signed acts in test-local batches of at most64 naming4097 absent members, inspect real count/bytes after each, then name @una again inside the same300-second window and require exactly one fresh read and the original accepted outcome. Real signatures, Native turns, SQLite and Membership answers stay real; the made-up observing platform definition is labelled. No shared fixture bound or deadline changes. One control restores unbounded insertion and must fail on actual map size. No second eviction test is proposed. The design draft is /private/tmp/artroom-r3b-design-review-20261109.md; source still waits for R3a's review request and your byte/custody ruling.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"planner"}}